			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828746">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>A bloodstained kirigami paper doll 1.56 meters in length drawn on to resemble a female human in an anime style, wearing gothic &quot;lolita&quot; style attire. Edges of the paper are abnormally sharp and capable of inflicting wounds on contact far greater than the amount of pressure and composition of the fibers would allow for. Subject is inanimate but believed to be sentient.</li>
<li>Any male who enters the doll's line of &quot;sight&quot; has an approximate 3% chance of being imprinted on, upon which its effect manifests. Upon entering REM sleep, the victim has a 50% chance to enter a state similar to sleep paralysis, in which a vision of the doll will appear to them and gently caress them, leaving deep wounds. This process is painless but can still result in complications from blood loss or infection.</li>
<li>Any female (biological or transgender) the victim interacts with that is not of blood relation enters a similar state the next time they sleep in which they are executed in a manner similar to the Chinese Lingchi. This process is not painless.</li>
<li>If the victim has not expired after a period of seven days, they will progress to Stage 2 in which they have an approximate 12.5% chance of the doll attempting to copulate with them. This normally results in death by blood loss. Only one affected victim can exist at a time.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Article proceeds normally, with an addendum regarding its recovery from the belongings of a deceased Japanese man implied to be its creator after his &quot;suicide&quot; in police custody. Several experiment logs are listed near the end with the Foundation using D-Class to determine how it works.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Final experiment log has the Foundation manage to keep a D-Class alive long enough to describe Stage 2 to them. He explains that the doll, which was silent before then, kept repeating a single phrase: &quot;Mō kakkoīdesu ka?&quot; (Japanese for &quot;Are we cool yet?&quot;)</p>

