			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831057">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Subject is inanimate but believed to be sentient.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why do they think the scp is sentient?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Any male who enters the doll's line of &quot;sight&quot; has an approximate 3% chance of being imprinted on, upon which its effect manifests. Upon entering REM sleep, the victim has a 50% chance to enter a state similar to sleep paralysis, in which a vision of the doll will appear to them and gently caress them, leaving deep wounds.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels like it'd be pretty uncommon to occur and it feels like it raises questions like 'how did anyone discover this' and 'why does it only affect 3% of people'?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Any female (biological or transgender) the victim interacts with that is not of blood relation enters a similar state the next time they sleep in which they are executed in a manner similar to the Chinese Lingchi. This process is not painless.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels&#8230;.weirdly cruel?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Article proceeds normally, with an addendum regarding its recovery from the belongings of a deceased Japanese man implied to be its creator after his &quot;suicide&quot; in police custody. Several experiment logs are listed near the end with the Foundation using D-Class to determine how it works.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So like&#8230;my concern here is that it feels like these experiment logs just won't really be interesting and they also feel like the kinda meat of this article? Like, the anomaly behaves in a way that's relatively straight forward and so I'm not sure what doing experiment logs adds to this beyond what's laid out in the description, y'know?</p>
<hr />
<p>At the end of the day, this feels&#8230;kinda needlessly edgy but without any kind of pay off to it. It leaves an unpleasant taste in my mouth, though I can't quite put my finger on why; but it also feels like you don't really <em>do</em> much with the concept: like, this feels like the kinda thing that could be a huge inspection of how e.g. westerners appropriate japanese culture, or like, investigating the role gender plays here or something like that but instead we just have a generic doll that effectively fucks you to death and I'm really not that into that played straight, y'know?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

